course: dictionary
lesson: 3447
title: Facile: too easy to be true
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Facile is an adjective, a word that describes a noun. Its main meaning is too simple: an idea said or done without careful thought, so it skips over the real problem. «A facile answer» sounds neat at first, but it does not really solve anything.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If a problem is said to be fixed by one quick sentence, and a teacher writes «facile» beside it, the teacher is criticising the answer, not praising it. Ask yourself: does this answer ignore the hard part? If it does, facile probably fits.
explain: There is also an old, literary meaning: done smoothly and easily, with no effort showing. You may meet it in older stories, where a facile style means skilful and effortless. The surrounding words will tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Facile is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «a facile answer».
fact: The main meaning is too simple, said without careful thought, and ignoring the real problem.
fact: The old meaning is done easily, smooth and effortless.
fact: In the phrase «C'est facile» (it's easy), facile means easy.
fact: Teachers often write facile as criticism when an answer is too shallow.
exercise: Which phrase from a debate means an answer that is too easy and shallow? | a kind answer | a loud answer | *a facile answer
exercise: Mrs Patel writes «facile» beside Sam's essay. What is she telling him? | His handwriting is hard to read | His answer is perfect and very clever | *His answer is too simple and ignores the real problem | His answer is far too long
exercise: In the French phrase «C'est facile», what does facile mean? | Far away | Hard to see | *Easy | Difficult
test: In an old story, a writer's style is called facile. What does this suggest? | Very loud | Too simple and rude | Done with great effort, slow and heavy | *Smooth and effortless, done with skill
test: Which sentence uses facile in its main meaning? | *The minister's facile solution ignored the real cause of the problem | The facile road wound up the mountain | Our dog is called Facile | We ate a facile lunch in the park
exam: A speaker in a debate says, «That is a facile solution.» What does the speaker mean? | *It is too simple and ignores the real problem | It is an easy game to play | It is a clever solution that solves everything | It is a solution written in French
